                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              be a regular semicategory. The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi RegPsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k:RegPsh(\mathcal{G})\to Prsh(\mathcal{G})
              defined on objects by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Nat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\mapsto Nat(Y_\mathcal{G}({}_-),F)
              is fully-faithful and part of an adjoint string
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi j
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi RegPsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Prsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i\dashv j\dashv k:RegPsh(\mathcal{G})\hookrightarrow Prsh(\mathcal{G})
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              identifying the regular presheaves with the Yoneda presheaves and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              identifying them with the presheaves that are colimits of representables.
          %p
            For the proof see Moens et al. (
            %a{:href => "#MBB02"}> 2002
            , p.179).
