          %h2#references References
          %p Regular semicategories were introduced in
          %ul
            %li#MBB02
              M.-A. Moens, U. Bernani-Canani,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"} F. Borceux
              %em On regular presheaves and regular semi-categories
              , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
              %strong XLIII
              no.3 (2002) pp.163-190. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_2002__43_3_163_0"}> numdam
              )
          %p Their quantaloid-enriched theory is studied in
          %ul
            %li#Stubbe05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isar+Stubbe"}> Isar Stubbe
              ,
              %em Categorical structures enriched in a quantaloid : regular presheaves, regular semicategories
              , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
              %strong XLVI
              no.2 (2005) pp.99-121. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_2005__46_2_99_0"}> numdam
              )
          %p For the origins in algebra of the concept see
          %ul
            %li
              F. Grandjean,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Vitale"} E. M. Vitale
              %em Morita equivalence for regular algebras
              , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
              %strong XXXIX
              (1998) pp.137-153. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1998__39_2_137_0"}> numdam
              )
